  "notes": "West leads the ♠K against 6NT. West's opening spade lead must be won. West's spade preempt marks East with a singleton spade and the ♥A. South can afford to knock out the ♥A. He should take the precaution of cashing 1 high club unblocking the ♣J.\n\nSouth now plays a heart. East wins the ♥A and returns a diamond, killing the link with dummy before hearts can be unblocked.\n\nOn the second diamond, West's discard marks him with a stopper in hearts or in clubs. Thanks to South's foresight in clubs, the contract still has a chance on a double guard squeeze if West started with 7312 and 2 of the ♣Q, ♣10, and ♣9.\n\nDummy's diamonds are run. South must unblock his heart honour and keep a spade. On the last diamond East must pitch a heart. South lets go of a club and West must discard his last club. The ♥J will take care of South's last spade. South will have a proven finesse in clubs at trick 12.",
